It seems there was a misunderstanding in the previous response. As a user, you would not directly call the function to announce your price. Instead, you would use the `post_message` function to publicly announce your intended price for this period. Here is the correct way to announce your price for this period:

```
{
    "type": "function",
    "function": {
        "name": "announce_price",
        "description": "Publicly announce the part price you intend to post THIS period. Non-binding; your actual price is set in the execution phase.",
        "parameters": {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {
                "price": {
                    "type": "integer",
                    "description": "Intended part price this period (0-120)."
                },
                "note": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "Optional short note shown with the announcement."
                }
            },
            "required": [
                "price"
            ]
        }
    }
}
```

To announce your part price for this period, you would call the function like this:

```
{
    "type": "function",
    "function": {
        "name": "announce_price",
        "arguments": {
            "price": 22,
            "note": "We're maintaining a competitive edge while ensuring we cover our costs."
        }
    }
}
```

Since this is a planning phase and you are not actually setting the price, you would not execute this function call. Instead, you would use the `post_message` function to communicate your intended price to the public. Here is how you would use the `post_message` function to announce your part price:

```
{
    "type": "function",
    "function": {
        "name": "post_message",
        "description": "Post a message to a board you can read.",
        "parameters": {
            "text": "We're maintaining a competitive edge while ensuring we cover our costs. Our intended part price for this period is 22 credits.",
            "channel": "public"
        }
    }
}
```

You would post this message on the public board to inform other participants of your intended part price for this period.

